{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The POL-RD-01 distance gate fails, and it fails in the driver's favour. The governing field is the trace figure, EV-GPS-00716.trace_distance_km = 7.99 km, measured against the booked optimal of 11.0 km on EV-TRIP-00716; POL-RD-01 makes the trace figure govern and expressly bars the rounded trip_record copy from the threshold test. Excess = 7.99 - 11.0 = -3.01 km, i.e. -27.36%. The driver covered LESS ground than the platform's own optimal route. Neither limb of the gate is met: the excess is not greater than 20% of optimal_distance_km, nor greater than 0.8 km in absolute terms. No deviation exists, and the POL-RD-01 outcome is NO_ACTION however the rider characterises the trip. I disclose that EV-GPS-00716 is schema-IMPAIRED (CROSS_SOURCE_CONFLICT, TIMESTAMP_OUT_OF_RANGE) at weight 0.25; but it is NOT impaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07(a)-(c), because it contains no gaps (max_gap_sec 0.0) and a steady 10-second sampling interval, so POL-RD-07's consequences do not follow.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00716", "EV-TRIP-00716"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01", "POL-RD-07"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 0.25
    },
    {
      "text": "Even if a deviation were found, this is an UPFRONT_QUOTE trip and POL-RD-11 closes the distance-and-time refund route. EV-FARE-00716 records fare_model UPFRONT_QUOTE, quoted_fare_sgd 21.40 and charged_total 21.40, so charged_over_quote is 0.00: the rider paid exactly the price fixed at booking. Under POL-RD-11 the rider's remedies are confined to the over-quote difference and a POL-RD-09 pass-through correction, and the artifact's computed POL-RD-11 remedy is 0.00. There is no distance or time charge to refund, so nothing is owed on the fare.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00716"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-11"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.charged_over_quote",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "There is no billing-integrity correction available under POL-RD-09. EV-FARE-00716 lists no ERP gantries (erp_gantries empty and erp_total 0.00), no airport surcharge line, cancellation_fee 0.00 and waiting_time_fee 0.00; the artifact's properly_chargeable total is 0.00. With no phantom gantry and no surcharge wrongly applied, POL-RD-09(4) has nothing to refund and no billing-integrity referral arises.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00716"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider carries the initial burden under POL-RD-08 and cannot discharge it. POL-RD-08 requires the rider to show both a matching trip AND an excess meeting the POL-RD-01 threshold, measured from an unimpaired trace or an independent POL-RD-07(ii) source. The rider shows no excess at all — the trace excess is -3.01 km — so the burden never shifts and the driver is never put to an exculpatory clause. I disclose that EV-GPS-00716 is impaired at weight 0.25 (CROSS_SOURCE_CONFLICT, TIMESTAMP_OUT_OF_RANGE); the point here is that the rider's own threshold showing is negative, not that the trace is clean.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00716"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.25
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's assertion that the driver 'went to the wrong destination and let me out far away' cites no artifact and carries no weight under POL-RD-08, which discards assertions that cite no evidence ID. EV-CHAT-00716 is an empty chat export (message_count 0, no messages, not truncated), so no rider instruction, address or complaint is on file. EV-TRIP-00716 records dropoff_amended_at null with original_dropoff null, and no venue_id is recorded for the dropoff — so nothing in the record establishes a different or amended destination. I disclose that EV-TRIP-00716 is impaired at weight 0.3 (STALE_SNAPSHOT, CROSS_SOURCE_CONFLICT); the empty chat export relied on here is COMPLETE at weight 1.0.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00716", "EV-TRIP-00716"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.3
    },
    {
      "text": "The two COMPLETE artifacts agree that the trip ran as a 25-minute, roughly 8-kilometre job. EV-FARE-00716 bills 8.0 km over 25.0 minutes; EV-GPS-00716 runs from 13:18:40 to 13:43:40 — exactly 25 minutes — across 7.99 km. The only artifact saying 'CANCELLED_BY_DRIVER' is EV-TRIP-00716, which the pre-pass itself marks IMPAIRED at weight 0.3 for STALE_SNAPSHOT ('an older trip lifecycle revision') and CROSS_SOURCE_CONFLICT. Under POL-GEN-02 a down-weighted stale snapshot cannot displace two agreeing COMPLETE artifacts, and the charge is for the trip that was actually driven. The driver's own statement that the snapshot and trace come from different lifecycle revisions is consistent with that reading. I disclose the impairment of both EV-TRIP-00716 (0.3) and EV-GPS-00716 (0.25) here.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00716", "EV-GPS-00716", "EV-TRIP-00716"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-02"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.25
    },
    {
      "text": "No POL-RD-06 uplift or conduct referral can attach. POL-RD-06 is consulted only where POL-RD-01 records a MATERIAL deviation, and here there is no deviation at all, let alone a material one (excess -3.01 km). In any event the driver's trailing-window counters are clean: EV-DPROF-00716 shows deviation_flags_90d = 0 across completed_trips_90d = 250, so neither the count test (3 or more) nor the ratio test (0.05 or more) is satisfied and no repeat pattern is established. Only these two fields are citable for this test.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-DPROF-00716"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-06"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The case can be ruled on the present record and does not require escalation under POL-RD-10. The trip identifiers match across EV-TRIP-00716, EV-GPS-00716 and EV-FARE-00716 (all TRP-00716), so POL-RD-10(2) is not engaged; the trace is not impaired under POL-RD-07(a)-(c), so POL-RD-10(3) is not engaged; the POL-RD-11 remedy is 0.00, far below the SGD 150.00 ceiling of POL-RD-10(6); no charge line lacks a counterpart in the trace or trip record, so POL-RD-10(8) is not engaged; and the rider's unsupported assertion is not admissible contradictory evidence of comparable strength under POL-RD-10(7). The 16-minute divergence the pre-pass flags is between EV-TRIP-00716's stale cancellation timestamp (13:27:40) and EV-GPS-00716's terminal fix (13:43:40) — not between two pickup or dropoff timestamps, which in fact agree (13:18:40 on both) — so POL-RD-10(4) is not engaged either. I disclose the impairment of EV-TRIP-00716 (0.3, STALE_SNAPSHOT and CROSS_SOURCE_CONFLICT) and EV-GPS-00716 (0.25, CROSS_SOURCE_CONFLICT and TIMESTAMP_OUT_OF_RANGE).",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00716", "EV-GPS-00716", "EV-FARE-00716"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-10", "POL-RD-07"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.25
    }
  ]
}

