  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "NO_ACTION",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.85,
    "explanation": "To both parties. Outcome: NO_ACTION. The SGD 21.40 charge stands and no money moves, from either side. The deciding facts, and what I did with each argument, are set out below. FARE (the deciding fact). This trip is an upfront-quoted fare. EV-FARE-00716 records fare_model UPFRONT_QUOTE, quoted_fare_sgd 21.40 and total_charged 21.40, so the charged-over-quote figure is 0.00; under POL-RD-11 no distance or time refund is available on an upfront fare and the clause's own remedy computes to 0.00. The same artifact shows no ERP gantries (erp_total 0.00), no airport surcharge, cancellation_fee 0.00 and waiting_time_fee 0.00, so POL-RD-09 has nothing to correct and no billing-integrity referral under POL-RD-09(4) arises. The driver's arguments on these two points are accepted. ROUTE DEVIATION. POL-RD-01 makes the trace figure govern. EV-GPS-00716 records trace_distance_km 7.99 against the booked optimal_distance_km of 11.0 on EV-TRIP-00716: an excess of -3.01 km (-27.36%). Both establishment tests require a positive excess, so neither is met and no deviation exists. A POL-RD-06 material-deviation uplift or conduct referral therefore cannot attach, and in any event the driver's trailing-window counters are clean (deviation_flags_90d 0 across completed_trips_90d 250 on EV-DPROF-00716), so no pattern is established. THE RIDER'S ACCOUNT. The assertion that the driver went to the wrong destination and set the rider down far away is not carried by any artifact. EV-CHAT-00716 is a complete but empty chat export (0 messages, not truncated), and EV-TRIP-00716 records dropoff_amended_at null, original_dropoff null and no venue, so no different or amended destination is established. The trace is also shorter than the optimal route, not longer; a shortfall does not meet the deviation gate, and on an upfront fare no distance refund follows however the trip is characterised. IMPAIRED ARTIFACTS, DISCLOSED. EV-GPS-00716 carries weight 0.25 with issue codes CROSS_SOURCE_CONFLICT and TIMESTAMP_OUT_OF_RANGE; EV-TRIP-00716 carries weight 0.30 with issue codes CROSS_SOURCE_CONFLICT and STALE_SNAPSHOT (an older lifecycle revision, whose recorded cancellation at 13:27:40 cannot displace the telemetry running to 13:43:40). Neither governs the result. The trace is not impaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07(a) to (c) - it has no gaps (max_gap_sec 0.0) and a steady 10-second sampling interval - so POL-RD-10(3) is not engaged and the pre-pass impairment is a POL-GEN-02 down-weight only. The fact the ruling actually rests on, that this is an upfront fare charged exactly at its quote with no chargeable pass-throughs, is carried by EV-FARE-00716 at weight 1.0. Under POL-GEN-02(2) the confidence cap is therefore 1.0, not the 0.30 the rider's advocate proposes; that escalation argument is rejected. NO ESCALATION. I checked the POL-RD-10 triggers. (2) the trip identifiers match (TRP-00716 on trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown). (3) the trace is not impaired under POL-RD-07(a) to (c). (4) the 16-minute divergence flagged by the pre-pass is between a cancellation event and the trace's terminal fix, not between pickup or dropoff timestamps - pickup agrees at 13:18:40 on both artifacts and ended_at is null - so (4) is not engaged. (5) no exculpatory clause is invoked against a missing or inadequate artifact. (6) the remedy is 0.00. (7) the rider's uncited assertion is not admissible contradictory evidence of comparable strength. (8) the charged distance and time lines have counterparts in the trace. Confidence is above the 0.70 floor, so the case is decided rather than escalated. REFERRALS. None. No clause produces one here: POL-RD-09(4) has no phantom line or misapplied surcharge, and POL-RD-06(c) has no material deviation and no repeat pattern. One open question belongs to the file rather than the referrals list: EV-TRIP-00716 is a stale lifecycle snapshot whose cancellation conflicts with the telemetry, and the payments side may wish to reconcile that snapshot's status against the fare record."
  },
